Description: Fix V4L2 stateful decoder instance counting
 The V4L2 stateful decoder keeps an instance count as several
 hardware decoders have a fixed upper limit of how many streams they
 can deal with. The current code has multiple places where the slot
 can be freed twice. e.g. if the instance count is exceeded the
 count is decremented immediately and again when the object is
 destroyed. Fix by keeping a flag that is set when the slot is claimed.
 .
 Fix v4l2_unittest to catch miscounting on fail in TooManyDecoderInstances
 Run the allocate until failure test twice to check that instances are
 correctly freed on destruction.
 .
